  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: fde9e6c05e247ec4ea9eba8397b000e3, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  subject: Shell Tools
  context: 'Shell tools are important prehistoric artifacts discovered at Balobok
    Rockshelter in Sanga-Sanga, Tawi-Tawi, Philippines. Some of these tools were
    made from giant clam shells and shaped into useful implements called shell adzes.
    These artifacts show how early inhabitants used natural materials from their
    coastal environment to create practical tools.


    Their craftsmanship demonstrates
    the resourcefulness and skills of ancient communities. Today, these discoveries
    help archaeologists understand the technology and way of life of prehistoric
    people in the Philippines.'
  logbookBook: {fileID: 1450703704}
